The complete target contract is documented in docs/product-contract.md and is not currently implemented or passing in full. The Phase 0 target contract pins Android NDK revision 29.0.14206865 exactly. Input is limited to 1 GiB, generated bytecode to 64 KiB per protected function, and one invocation to 4096 functions. The entry ABI permits at most 8 integer or pointer arguments and a result of either void or one integer or pointer value.

Production randomness defaults to crypto/rand. An explicit seed is for debug/test only and is never reported. Input, output, and report paths are distinct; the default is no-clobber, and -force uses atomic same-directory temporary-file replacement.

Instruction translation, CFG construction, and ELF parsing or rewriting use fail-closed handling for unsupported, malformed, ambiguous, or invalid input. Physical-device release gates cover API 23+, 4 KiB and 16 KiB page sizes, BTI, PAC, dynamic-linker loading, and transformed execution; they are not currently claimed as passing.

Report v1 has schema_version: 1. It is the TARGET Phase 2 contract and is not yet fully implemented by the current report emitter.
